 "note": [
  "Scripture is the Bíblia Livre para o Mundo (por_bpm), pasted by script where Clement’s quotation agrees with it in sense. Clement quotes the Septuagint; where its sense differs (Dt 32:15, Is 1:16-20, most of Is 53, Ps 50, Job 5:17-26, Pv 1:23-31 and others) his wording is rendered and marked self-rendered, and Sl 32:2 is adapted to his «em cuja boca». Pasted verses keep the Bíblia Livre’s own você and SENHOR beside Clement’s vós.",
  "AI-translated (job #5229) in parallel chapters, then reconciled: the Corinthians are vós; pronouns for God are capitalised in Clement’s prose as in the English; names follow the Portuguese Bible tradition (Raabe, Enoque, Ló, Davi, Danaides e Dirces). English slips noted: “Thou shall” (shalt), “and there would be strife” (that). Awaiting native review."
 ],
